{"id":"sig-sauer-p320","slug":"sig-sauer-p320","name":"SIG Sauer P320","aliases":["SIG P320","SIG P-320","SIG-Sauer P320","SIG-Sauer P-320","SIG Sauer P-320"],"kind":"firearm","category":"pistols","subcategory":"Semi-automatic pistol","description":"The SIG Sauer P320 is a modular striker-fired semi-automatic pistol made by SIG Sauer, Inc., SIG Sauer's American branch. It marked Sig Sauer's first foray into striker-fired pistols, as their first offering on the commercial market.","history":"The P320 chambered in 9×19mm Parabellum was introduced in the North American market on 15 January 2014, followed by the .45 ACP compact model at the SHOT Show in January 2015.\nOn 19 January 2017, it was announced that a customized version of the SIG Sauer P320 had won the United States Army's XM17 Modular Handgun System competition. In April 2017, Caracal International was made a licensed producer for the P320.\nIn December 2025, the SIG Sauer P320 replaced the SIG P220 as the Swiss Army's new service pistol.","development":"The P320 is a further development of the SIG Sauer P250, utilizing a striker-fired mechanism in lieu of a double action only hammer system. SIG lists the trigger pull of the standard P320 at 29 N (6.5 lbf). The P320 trigger pull is accomplished by a combination of a tensioned striker spring, ideal trigger shoe and trigger bar dimensions, sear/striker engagement, and a balanced trigger system.","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"Cartridge & Action","items":[{"label":"Cartridge","value":"9×19mm Parabellum"},{"label":"Action","value":"Short recoil-operated, locked-breech SIG Sauer system"},{"label":"Feed System","value":"10-round magazine .45 ACP"},{"label":"Feed System","value":"14-round magazine .357 SIG, .40 S&W"},{"label":"Feed System","value":"12-round, 15-round, 17-round, 21-round, or 30 round 9×19mm Parabellum"},{"label":"Sights","value":"Fixed iron sights, front—blade, rear—notch, with optional tritium night inserts, optical reflex sight on RX models, high sights on RX and Tacops models"}]},{"group":"Dimensions","items":[{"label":"Weight","value":"833 g (incl. magazine)","numeric":833,"unit":"g"},{"label":"Length","value":"203 mm","numeric":203,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Barrel Length","value":"120 mm","numeric":120,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Width","value":"35.5 mm","numeric":35.5,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Height","value":"140 mm","numeric":140,"unit":"mm"}]},{"group":"Production","items":[{"label":"Designer","value":"Sean Toner"},{"label":"Designer","value":"Michael W. Mayerl"},{"label":"Designed","value":"2014"},{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"[[SIG Sauer#SIG Sauer Inc."},{"label":"Produced","value":"2014–present"}]},{"group":"Service","items":[{"label":"Origin","value":"United States"},{"label":"In Service","value":"2014–present"}]}],"specIndex":{"Cartridge":"9×19mm Parabellum","Action":"Short recoil-operated, locked-breech SIG Sauer system","Feed System":"10-round magazine .45 ACP","Sights":"Fixed iron sights, front—blade, rear—notch, with optional tritium night inserts, optical reflex sight on RX models, high sights on RX and Tacops models","Weight":"833 g (incl. magazine)","Length":"203 mm","Barrel Length":"120 mm","Width":"35.5 mm","Height":"140 mm","Designer":"Sean Toner","Designed":"2014","Manufacturer":"[[SIG Sauer#SIG Sauer Inc.","Produced":"2014–present","Origin":"United States","In Service":"2014–present"},"images":{"hero":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7a/Sig_Sauer_P320_Modular_Handgun_System.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sig_Sauer_P320_Modular_Handgun_System.jpg","width":2791,"height":2271,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"Digitallymade"},"thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Sig_Sauer_P320_Modular_Handgun_System.jpg/330px-Sig_Sauer_P320_Modular_Handgun_System.jpg"},"gallery":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7a/Sig_Sauer_P320_